dsh-zhipu-plan README · What it adds：- **Zhipu-backed web search, page reading, and GitHub documentation (Zhipu MCP), as additional tools.** The same coding-plan credential the sign-in stores also powers three capabilities, so there is no second key to enter — and none of them replaces a built-in tool:
  - `zhipu_web_search`, mounted globally while the **search** switch is on (default **on**), accepts one to four focused queries, runs them concurrently, and merges the sources round-robin (URL-deduped, capped at 40) — the upstream backend hard-caps **ten results per query** and takes no count parameter. The built-in `web_search` keeps running on its shipped backend;
  - `zhipu_web_fetch`, mounted globally while the **reader** switch is on (default **on**), reads one page through Zhipu's web reader (markdown, images dropped, 200,000-character clamp, untrusted-content boundary) — the built-in `web_fetch` is likewise untouched;
  - `github_search_doc`, `github_get_repo_structure`, and `github_read_file` expose Zhipu's zread server, mounted globally while the **zread** switch is on (default **off**); minimal-preset agents are masked off whatever additional tools are currently mounted, a
